    "patchSets": [
        {
            "number": 1,
            "revision": "227e613b830d87f4c5a36f70a1fa6a174f175d69",
            "parents": [
                "ebe4c574caac9dfd8b2754bda51c0cf869f1978f"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/41/78241/1",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                "username": "PrithviPai24"
            },
            "createdOn": 1739524979,
            "author": {
                "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                "username": "PrithviPai24"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Why do you need this? \nWhy does an empty bios cause problems? \nIf you had a system without PCIe devices, does an empty PCIe device collection cause problems ? \nIf you had a system without DIMMs, does an empty DIMM collection cause problems?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "1) In some platform where bmc is not managing bios. Performing a GET on /Systems/<>/Bios would throw error\n2) Adding a check before creating resource would help us to conditionally add the resource.\n3) Would help us avoid performing action such as bios password change or reset on non-existing resource"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "1)  Today when \"some platform where bmc is not managing bios. Performing a GET on /Systems/<>/Bios would throw error\" sounds like a bug.. If the system doesn't support Bios, it should return an empty collection\n\nCan you add more about this path /xyz/openbmc_project/bios_config/manager ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "Bios resource is not a collection. \nActions of the resource such as Reset, Change Password would throw error when bios-settings-manager service is not running (https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/redfish-core/lib/bios.hpp#L111)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Where is the Change Password action? \n\nWhat if we leave those actions off? Instead of leaving the whole resource off ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, we can do this. \nI will add check in respective function instead of whole resource."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "This breaks us. \nhttps://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/ebe4c574caac9dfd8b2754bda51c0cf869f1978f/redfish-core/lib/bios.hpp#L62\nWe have host (bios) firmware that isn't using /xyz/openbmc_project/bios_config/manager"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "yes, thanks for pointing out. \nAdding check here also would help right ? Can I take that path ? \nIf there is any better way please suggest I can try and test that approach."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't work because not everyone using Bios is using that path \n/xyz/openbmc_project/bios_config/manager\n\nWhat app is putting that out ? Can you add more to the commit msg about this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "https://github.com/openbmc/bios-settings-mgr is initializing that path. \nbios-settings-manager is responsible for BMC-BIOS communication. \nhttps://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-dbus-interfaces/blob/master/yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/BIOSConfig/Manager.interface.yaml exposes methods to reset bios, change bios password etc. \nIf `xyz.openbmc_project.biosconfig_manager.service` does not exists we would end up throwing internalError. This patch checks if the dbusPath exists and then allow operations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "What about Bios/host firmware https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/ebe4c574caac9dfd8b2754bda51c0cf869f1978f/redfish-core/lib/bios.hpp#L62  \nwhich in our case doesn't use https://github.com/openbmc/bios-settings-mgr ?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
                    "line": 3083,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Prithvi Pai",
                        "email": "prithvi24pai@gmail.com",
                        "username": "PrithviPai24"
                    },
                    "message": "yes for boot related operations and bios version related information we don't use bios-seting-manager"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/systems.hpp",
